From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregor MacLennan <gmaclennan@awana.digital>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 19:20:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] src: skip unclonable env vars on Android
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

KVStore::Clone() treats a name that enumerates but doesn't resolve as
fatal, returning a null store — and the bionic linker strips variables
like LD_PRELOAD from a starting app, making that combination real on
Android. Skip the unresolvable variable instead of losing the whole
clone; a default-env Worker is the visible consumer. Covered by
test/parallel/test-mobile-worker-env-clone.

Co-authored-by: Jaime Bernardo <jaime@janeasystems.com>
---
 src/node_env_var.cc | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/node_env_var.cc b/src/node_env_var.cc
index 5550a4bee3..761fc10b23 100644
--- a/src/node_env_var.cc
+++ b/src/node_env_var.cc
@@ -235,7 +235,9 @@ std::shared_ptr<KVStore> KVStore::Clone(Isolate* isolate) const {
     }
     CHECK(key->IsString());
     if (!Get(isolate, key.As<String>()).ToLocal(&value)) {
-      return nullptr;
+      // On Android, it's possible that some environment variables get removed,
+      // such as LD_PRELOAD. Skip them rather than aborting the whole clone.
+      continue;
     }
     copy->Set(isolate, key.As<String>(), value.As<String>());
   }
